      "text": "To determine the greatest possible three-digit number that is divisible by both 3 and 6, we need to recognize that any number divisible by 6 is also divisible by 3. Therefore, we only need to find the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6.\n\nFirst, identify the greatest three-digit number, which is 999. We need to find the largest integer \\( n \\) such that \\( 6n \\) is a three-digit number. This means \\( 6n < 1000 \\). To find \\( n \\), we divide 999 by 6:\n\n\\[\nn = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{999}{6} \\right\\rfloor\n\\]\n\nCalculating the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{999}{6} = 166.5\n\\]\n\nThe greatest integer less than or equal to 166.5 is 166. Therefore, the greatest three-digit number that is divisible by 6 is:\n\n\\[\n6 \\times 166 = 996\n\\]\n\nTo confirm, we check that 996 is divisible by both 3 and 6. Since 996 is even, it is divisible by 2. To check for divisibility by 3, we sum the digits of 996:\n\n\\[\n9 + 9 + 6 = 24\n\\]\n\nSince 24 is divisible by 3, 996 is divisible by 3. Since 996 is a multiple of 6, we have confirmed that 996 is divisible by both 3 and 6.\n\nThus, the greatest possible three-digit number that is divisible by 3 and 6 is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{996}\n\\]",
